# docs/orphans-allow — the declared EXPECTED live-orphan census (WI-228).
#
# Read by scripts/check_docs.py. A "live orphan" is a doc no navigation path
# reaches from an entry root. Most orphans are RETAINED EVIDENCE — reviews,
# closed-WI specs, round artifacts, registry entries that happen to be Markdown
# — which must stay on disk yet is not a navigation node: "unlinked-from-
# navigation" is the wrong frame for it.
#
# Each non-comment line is a shell glob (fnmatch, repo-relative POSIX; `*` spans
# separators, so `docs/reviews/*` classifies the whole subtree). A matched
# orphan is EXPECTED: dropped from the per-doc warnings, replaced by one
# aggregate `note`, and never a finding even under `--strict-orphans`. An
# orphan matching NOTHING here is GENUINE — it warns, which is the
# newly-introduced-orphan ratchet: link it, index it, or, if it is a new
# evidence class, add its glob here WITH ITS REASON.
#
# This is a DECLARATION, not a suppression list. Every line carries why, so a
# genuinely undiscoverable new doc cannot hide inside a steady wall of expected
# ones — the silent-growth mode every declared list in this kit exists to bound.
# Deleting the file restores the pre-declaration behavior (every orphan warns).

# The work-item registry's spec-folder home: each file IS a registry entry, not
# a page anyone navigates to (its `id` and its DIRECTORY are what tools read).
# Linking hundreds of them into the doc graph would bury the navigation the
# graph exists to check. Their links are still validated like any other doc.
docs/work/*

# The log's fragment drop-box: a work branch's `docs/log.md` entry, parked under
# its own unique name until `scripts/trunk_step.py` compiles it into the log on
# the trunk. Transient by construction and never a navigation node — the entry
# becomes reachable the moment it lands in `log.md`, and the fragment is deleted.
docs/log.d/*

# Per-close reports (docs/handbacks/README.md). A report is IMMUTABLE evidence
# whose PATH is the close event's identity — never edited, never deleted, and
# never linked from a navigation node, because the thing that makes it reachable
# as work is the disposition row intake mints against it, not a doc link.
# Retained-evidence class, same as docs/archive/specs/*.
docs/handbacks/*
